/-
# Graphplay.Dowsing.Conjecture93

**Hole D2 (Round 2): Conjecture 9.3 of `quasi_infinite_adjoint_v2`.**

The statement, paraphrased from §9 *Connections and Open Directions* of the
v2 manuscript:

> A family of finite weighted graphs `(G_n, P_n)` with **consistent**
> equitable partitions admits **both** a graphon limit (Theorem 5.5 / our
> `Graphon.Limit`) **and** a chiral signing speedup on the same partition
> (Theorem 7.1 / our `Chiral.signedBy_preserves_equitable`) **iff** the
> Bose-Mesner algebra of the limit object coincides with the algebra
> generated by the characteristic projections of the limit partition.

This file does four things:

1. Gives a precise Lean Prop for the conjecture in the form
   `Conjecture93 F = (graphon_half F ∧ chiral_half F) ↔ algebra_eq F`,
   with each predicate defined from already-existing canonical types
   (`ConsistentPartitionSequence`, `BoseMesner`,
   `EquitablePartition.projector`, `coherentAlgebra`).

2. Decomposes the conjecture into forward and reverse implications and
   states each as a separate (sorried) theorem.

3. Constructs **six test families** — five expected positive instances and
   one tightness/counterexample candidate — and for each gives a `Prop`
   tagging which side of the iff is asserted. Each family is currently a
   stub (the underlying graphs are well-defined; the equitable conditions
   are sorried).

4. States the two clean **sufficient conditions** as corollaries (algebra
   equality alone, and association-scheme-uniformity) and the four
   currently-known failure modes (necessary conditions).

5. Distinguishes a **strong** version (any unitary signing) from a **weak**
   version (`U(1)` phases / cross-constant signings only). The weak version
   is precisely what `Chiral.signedBy_preserves_equitable` certifies; the
   strong version permits the larger nonabelian signing space of
   Levine et al. (2605.04414) — and the weak version is the one we
   conjecture to be equivalent to algebra coincidence.

## Citations

* §9.3 of `paper/quasi_infinite_adjoint_v2.typ` — the original conjecture
  formulation.
* Levine, Mesapam, Mustico, Tamon, Tucker, Zhan,
  arXiv:2605.04414 (2026) — chiral signings and the `K_n^σ` speedup
  (`K_n^σ` test family below; tower 2).
* Chan, Coutinho, Tamon, Vinet, Zhan,
  arXiv:1907.04729 (2019) — fractional revival and association schemes;
  this is the *positive* template, where the Bose-Mesner algebra and the
  partition-projector algebra coincide and both halves hold.
* Xie, Tamon,
  arXiv:2301.07251 (2023) — the "no infinite tail" graphon limit
  family `K_n + path_n`; this is the candidate counterexample (graphon
  limit exists but the limit Bose-Mesner algebra is strictly larger than
  the partition-projector algebra of the tail).
* Borgs-Chayes-Lovász-Sós-Vesztergombi style cut-norm graphon convergence,
  see `Graphplay/Graphon/Limit.lean`.

Every nontrivial proof here is `sorry`. The file is a *specification*; the
intent of the round-2 exploration is to nail down (i) the right statement,
(ii) where it is known to hold, and (iii) where it is suspected to fail.
-/

import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Hermitian
import Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic
import Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Algebra.MatrixExponential
import Graphplay.Weighted
import Graphplay.Equitable
import Graphplay.Chiral
import Graphplay.QuantumGraph
import Graphplay.Graphon
import Graphplay.Graphon.Equitable
import Graphplay.Graphon.Limit

universe u v w

open scoped Matrix BigOperators
open MeasureTheory

namespace Graphplay
namespace Conjecture93

/-! ## 1. Ingredients

We assemble the conjecture out of objects already in the codebase:

* `ConsistentPartitionSequence I` — sequences `(G_n, P_n)` with embeddings
  `V_n ↪ V_{n+1}` respecting the cell map. (Graphon/Limit.lean.)
* `Graphon` and `GraphonEquitablePartition` — the limit object.
* `coherentAlgebra` / `BoseMesner` — Tower-3 algebras (QuantumGraph.lean).
* `EquitablePartition.projector` — the Tower-1↔Tower-3 bridge.
* `ChiralSigning`, `ChiralSigning.CrossConstant`,
  `WeightedGraph.signedBy_preserves_equitable` — Tower 2.
-/

variable {I : Type v} [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I]

/-- A **finite-stage Bose-Mesner candidate**.  At stage `n`, the
Bose-Mesner-style algebra of `(𝒮.G n, 𝒮.cells n)` is the smallest
unital `*`-subalgebra of `Matrix (𝒮.V n) (𝒮.V n) ℂ` containing both the
adjacency `(𝒮.G n).adj` and the partition projector for `𝒮.cells n`.

In the limit, this becomes the Bose-Mesner algebra of the limit graphon
quotient (the conjecture asserts this coincides with the partition
projector algebra). -/
noncomputable def finiteAdjAlgebra
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) (n : ℕ) :
    Submodule ℂ (Matrix (𝒮.V n) (𝒮.V n) ℂ) :=
  haveI := 𝒮.finV n
  haveI := 𝒮.decV n
  coherentAlgebra (𝒮.G n)

/-- The **partition-projector algebra** at stage `n`: the unital subalgebra
of `Matrix (𝒮.V n) (𝒮.V n) ℂ` generated by the partition projector
`Π_{P_n}` of the cell map `𝒮.cells n`.

Concretely, by `tower3_equitable_partition`, this is the algebra of
matrices that are *constant on each cell-pair block*; equivalently, the
image of the embedding `Matrix I I ℂ ↪ Matrix (𝒮.V n) (𝒮.V n) ℂ` that
inflates a quotient matrix to a cell-uniform matrix on `V n`. -/
noncomputable def partitionProjectorAlgebra
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) (n : ℕ) :
    Submodule ℂ (Matrix (𝒮.V n) (𝒮.V n) ℂ) :=
  -- the linear span of all matrices that are cell-pair constant.
  Submodule.span ℂ
    { M : Matrix (𝒮.V n) (𝒮.V n) ℂ |
        ∃ q : I → I → ℂ, ∀ x y, M x y = q (𝒮.cells n x) (𝒮.cells n y) }

/-! ## 2. The two halves of the conjecture

We give precise propositional content to "(a) admits a graphon limit on the
partition" and "(b) admits a chiral signing speedup on the partition".

For (a), we take the conclusion of
`ConsistentPartitionSequence.limit_exists`, which already lives in
`Graphplay.Graphon.Limit`. For (b), we take the existence of a *nontrivial*
chiral signing — `CrossConstant` on the cells of `P_n` for every `n`, with
the signed quotient evolving strictly faster (`τ_signed < τ_unsigned`) than
the unsigned bundle, in the sense of cell-uniform mixing.

We **don't** unfold "strictly faster mixing time" here; we package it as a
predicate `ChiralSpeedupOnQuotient` taking the cross-constant signing as
data. The intent is that the proof of either direction of Conjecture 9.3
will use this predicate via `Chiral.chiral_mixing_optimization`.
-/

/-- A `ConsistentPartitionSequence` **admits a graphon limit on its
partition** if the limit theorem `ConsistentPartitionSequence.limit_exists`
applies *and* the limit graphon equitable partition has the same fixed
index type `I` (i.e. no cells merge or split in the limit). -/
def admitsGraphonLimit (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  ∃ (Ω : Type u) (_ : MeasurableSpace Ω) (μ : Measure Ω)
    (W_∞ : Graphon Ω μ)
    (P_∞ : @GraphonEquitablePartition Ω _ μ I _ _ W_∞),
    Filter.Tendsto (fun n => 𝒮.quotient n) Filter.atTop (nhds P_∞.quotient)

/-- A `ConsistentPartitionSequence` **admits a chiral speedup on its
partition** if there exists a sequence of nontrivial chiral signings
`s_n`, each cross-constant on `𝒮.cells n`, which is *consistent* under
the embedding `𝒮.embed n` (so phases pull back) and whose signed quotient
evolves with a *strictly faster* (or, more weakly: *quantitatively
different*) cell-uniform mixing/PST time than the unsigned quotient.

We package the existence of a consistent cross-constant signing only;
"strictly faster" is left as a placeholder `True` predicate in the same
spirit as `Bundle.CellUniformMixing`. -/
def admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  ∃ s : ∀ n, ChiralSigning (𝒮.V n),
    (∀ n, (s n).CrossConstant (𝒮.cells n)) ∧
    -- consistency: phases pull back along the embedding
    (∀ n (x y : 𝒮.V n),
      (s (n + 1)).σ (𝒮.embed n x) (𝒮.embed n y) = (s n).σ x y) ∧
    -- "nontrivial": not the all-ones signing at every stage
    (∃ n x y, (s n).σ x y ≠ 1) ∧
    -- "speedup" predicate (placeholder; see Chiral.chiral_mixing_optimization)
    True

/-! ## 3. Algebra equality

The right-hand side of the conjecture: the finite-stage adjacency algebra
equals the partition-projector algebra at every (sufficiently large) stage.

The strongest form — equality at *every* stage — is what is needed for
the limit graphon's Bose-Mesner to equal the partition-projector algebra
of `P_∞`; convergence of submodules in operator-norm topology then takes
care of the limit step.
-/

/-- The **algebra-coincidence condition** at stage `n`: the smallest
coherent algebra containing `(𝒮.G n).adj` equals the partition-projector
algebra of `𝒮.cells n`. -/
def algebraCoincidence
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) (n : ℕ) : Prop :=
  finiteAdjAlgebra 𝒮 n = partitionProjectorAlgebra 𝒮 n

/-- The **(eventual) algebra-coincidence condition**: equality holds at
all sufficiently large stages. -/
def eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  ∃ N, ∀ n ≥ N, algebraCoincidence 𝒮 n

/-! ## 4. The conjecture, in two strengths

We give the **weak** version (the one we believe is true) and the
**strong** version (any unitary signing on `Matrix (V n) (V n) ℂ`, not just
cross-constant on cells).

The weak version is what `signedBy_preserves_equitable` certifies the
chiral half of; the strong version is open even in the finite case.
-/

/-- **Conjecture 9.3 (weak form).** A consistent partition sequence admits
both a graphon limit on its partition and a *cross-constant* chiral
speedup on the same partition iff its Bose-Mesner-style finite algebras
coincide with the partition-projector algebras at all sufficiently large
stages. -/
def Conjecture93_weak (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  (admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 ∧ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮)
    ↔ eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence 𝒮

/-- A *general* chiral signing speedup: existence of nontrivial unitary
signings at every stage, *not necessarily cross-constant on the cells*. -/
def admitsAnyChiralSpeedupOnPartition
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  ∃ s : ∀ n, ChiralSigning (𝒮.V n),
    (∃ n x y, (s n).σ x y ≠ 1) ∧
    True

/-- **Conjecture 9.3 (strong form).** With *any* (not necessarily
cross-constant) unitary signing standing in for the chiral half. This is
**not** equivalent to algebra coincidence in general — see the
counterexample family below. -/
def Conjecture93_strong (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  (admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 ∧ admitsAnyChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮)
    ↔ eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence 𝒮

/-! ## 5. Decomposition into forward and reverse implications -/

/-- **Forward direction (weak):** algebra coincidence implies both halves.
This is the easier direction: a Bose-Mesner algebra acts diagonally
across cells, so chiral signings respecting the partition descend to
phase-multiplications on the quotient, which is the speedup mechanism. -/
theorem conjecture93_weak_forward
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) :
    eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence 𝒮 →
      admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 ∧ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮 := by
  sorry

/-- **Reverse direction (weak):** the existence of a chiral speedup on the
partition **and** a graphon limit on the same partition forces the
Bose-Mesner algebra to coincide with the partition-projector algebra.

This is the hard direction. The expected proof: the chiral speedup
constraint forces `(𝒮.G n).adj` to lie in a *commutative* subalgebra of
`Matrix (V n) (V n) ℂ` that contains the partition projector; the graphon
limit then forces this subalgebra to be at most the partition-projector
algebra. -/
theorem conjecture93_weak_reverse
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) :
    (admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 ∧ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮) →
      eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence 𝒮 := by
  sorry

/-- Putting the two halves together. -/
theorem conjecture93_weak_iff
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) :
    Conjecture93_weak 𝒮 := by
  refine Iff.intro ?fwd ?rev
  · intro h
    exact conjecture93_weak_reverse 𝒮 h
  · intro h
    exact conjecture93_weak_forward 𝒮 h

/-! ## 6. Sufficient conditions (corollaries of the forward direction) -/

/-- **Corollary.** If `algebraCoincidence` holds at every stage, both
halves of the conjecture hold. -/
theorem both_halves_of_algebra_coincidence
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I)
    (h : ∀ n, algebraCoincidence 𝒮 n) :
    admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 ∧ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮 := by
  apply conjecture93_weak_forward
  exact ⟨0, fun n _ => h n⟩

/-- **Association scheme uniformity:** an additional assumption on the
sequence that each `(𝒮.G n)` lies in the Bose-Mesner algebra of an
association scheme **refining** the partition `𝒮.cells n`. Schemes are
parametrized by `d n : ℕ`. -/
def AssocSchemeUniform
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  ∀ n, ∃ d : ℕ,
    haveI := 𝒮.finV n
    haveI := 𝒮.decV n
    Nonempty (AssociationScheme (𝒮.V n) d)

/-- **Corollary.** Association-scheme-uniform sequences satisfy
algebra coincidence at every stage (Bose-Mesner = partition-projector
when the scheme classes refine the partition), hence both halves of
Conjecture 9.3 hold. -/
theorem both_halves_of_assocSchemeUniform
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I)
    (_h : AssocSchemeUniform 𝒮) :
    admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 ∧ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮 := by
  -- Bose-Mesner of the refining scheme contains the adjacency and the
  -- partition projector; commutativity then forces equality of the
  -- two algebras at every stage.
  sorry

/-! ## 7. Necessary conditions (failure modes that block one half) -/

/-- **Failure mode A:** if the chiral signing at stage `n` *fails*
`CrossConstant`, the chiral half is blocked because
`signedBy_preserves_equitable` does not apply: the signed graph need not
have `P_n` as an equitable partition. -/
theorem chiral_half_blocked_if_not_crossConstant
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I)
    (h : ¬ ∃ s : ∀ n, ChiralSigning (𝒮.V n),
         ∀ n, (s n).CrossConstant (𝒮.cells n)) :
    ¬ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮 := by
  intro ⟨s, hcc, _, _, _⟩
  exact h ⟨s, hcc⟩

/-- **Failure mode B (graphon half):** if the quotient matrices `𝒮.quotient n`
do not converge in operator norm, the graphon half fails. -/
theorem graphon_half_blocked_if_quotients_diverge
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I)
    (h : ¬ ∃ Q∞ : Matrix I I ℂ,
         Filter.Tendsto (fun n => 𝒮.quotient n) Filter.atTop (nhds Q∞)) :
    ¬ admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 := by
  intro ⟨_, _, _, _, P_∞, hP⟩
  exact h ⟨P_∞.quotient, hP⟩

/-- **Failure mode C:** if the Bose-Mesner-style algebra strictly contains
the partition-projector algebra at infinitely many stages, the right-hand
side of the conjecture fails. -/
def algebra_strictly_larger (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  ∀ N, ∃ n ≥ N, partitionProjectorAlgebra 𝒮 n < finiteAdjAlgebra 𝒮 n

theorem rhs_blocked_if_algebra_strictly_larger
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I)
    (h : algebra_strictly_larger 𝒮) :
    ¬ eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence 𝒮 := by
  intro ⟨N, hN⟩
  obtain ⟨n, hn, hlt⟩ := h N
  have heq := hN n hn
  exact absurd heq (ne_of_lt hlt).symm

/-- **Failure mode D (chiral half):** if every nontrivial chiral signing
breaks the equitable partition, then no speedup-on-partition can exist
because the proper analogue of `signedBy_preserves_equitable` fails. -/
def every_nontrivial_signing_breaks_partition
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I) : Prop :=
  ∀ n (s : ChiralSigning (𝒮.V n)),
    (∃ x y, s.σ x y ≠ 1) → ¬ s.CrossConstant (𝒮.cells n)

theorem chiral_half_blocked_if_every_signing_breaks
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I)
    (h : every_nontrivial_signing_breaks_partition 𝒮) :
    ¬ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮 := by
  intro ⟨s, hcc, _, ⟨n, x, y, hne⟩, _⟩
  exact h n (s n) ⟨x, y, hne⟩ (hcc n)

/-! ## 8. Test families

We list six explicit families and the `Prop` indicating which side of the
iff each is conjectured to satisfy. Underlying graph constructions are
straightforward; the equitable / consistency / chiral-signing axioms are
left as `sorry`. The intent is to make each family a concrete obstacle
or witness for the conjecture.
-/

/-! ### 8.1. `K_n^σ`: chirally-signed complete graphs (Levine et al. 2605.04414).

Partition: trivial (single cell). Both halves hold: the partition-projector
algebra is `ℂ · J + ℂ · I` (the trivial scheme), the Bose-Mesner of `K_n^σ`
is also `ℂ · I + ℂ · J` for the constant chiral signing.
-/

/-- The trivial single-cell partition sequence on `Fin n` with the unsigned
complete graph at every stage and the trivial all-zero embedding. The
Levine et al. chiral signing is applied externally; this family is just
the underlying sequence. -/
noncomputable def Kn_constSign (n : ℕ → ℕ) (hn : ∀ k, 0 < n k)
    (h_embed : ∀ k, n k ≤ n (k + 1)) :
    ConsistentPartitionSequence (I := Unit) (u := 0) where
  V := fun k => Fin (n k)
  finV := fun _ => inferInstance
  decV := fun _ => inferInstance
  measV := fun _ => ⊤
  msingV := fun _ => by infer_instance
  G := fun k =>
    { adj := fun x y => if x = y then 0 else 1
      herm := by sorry
      loopless := fun _ => by simp }
  cells := fun _ _ => ()
  embed := fun k x => ⟨x.val, lt_of_lt_of_le x.isLt (h_embed k)⟩
  embed_cells := fun _ _ => rfl
  equitable := by sorry

/-- **Claim (test family 1).** `K_n^σ` with the trivial single-cell partition
satisfies the conjecture: both halves hold, and algebra coincidence holds
(both algebras equal `ℂ · I + ℂ · J`). -/
theorem Kn_constSign_satisfies_conj93
    (n : ℕ → ℕ) (hn : ∀ k, 0 < n k) (h_embed : ∀ k, n k ≤ n (k + 1)) :
    Conjecture93_weak (Kn_constSign n hn h_embed) := by
  -- Both halves of the iff are *true* for this family, so the iff holds.
  -- LHS: graphon limit is the constant kernel `1` on `[0, 1]^2 \ diag`;
  --      cross-constant chiral signing is just a constant phase on the
  --      single cell, e.g. the Levine K_4 signing for n = 4.
  -- RHS: at every stage, both algebras equal `ℂ · I + ℂ · J`.
  sorry

/-! ### 8.2. Hamming graphs `H(n, q)` with chiral signing (Hamming scheme).

Partition: distance partition from `0^n`. Hamming scheme classes refine
the distance partition; algebra coincidence is *exact* (the Bose-Mesner
of the Hamming scheme equals the algebra of cell-pair-constant matrices
on `H(n, q)`). The Hamming scheme is association-scheme-uniform.
-/

/-- The Hamming-graph partition sequence `H(n, q)` indexed by `n` with `q`
fixed: vertex set `(Fin q)^n`, edges between strings differing in exactly
one coordinate, partition by Hamming weight (distance from `0^n`). -/
noncomputable def Hammingq (q : ℕ) (hq : 0 < q) :
    ConsistentPartitionSequence (I := ℕ) (u := 0) := by
  sorry

/-- **Claim (test family 2).** Hamming graphs with their distance partition
satisfy the conjecture. Algebra coincidence holds (Bose-Mesner of the
Hamming scheme equals the cell-pair-constant algebra). -/
theorem Hammingq_satisfies_conj93 (q : ℕ) (hq : 0 < q) :
    Conjecture93_weak (Hammingq q hq) := by
  sorry

/-! ### 8.3. `K_n + path_n` (Xie-Tamon 2301.07251).

Partition: distance-from-`K_n` (a `ℕ`-indexed cell map). Graphon limit
**does** exist (cf. `Graphon.Limit`); chiral speedup on the partition
**does not** exist because the path tail's Bose-Mesner algebra is the
*full* tridiagonal algebra at each `n`, strictly larger than the
partition-projector algebra of the distance cells.

This is the **candidate counterexample**: graphon half holds, chiral half
fails, hence LHS is false. The conjecture says RHS is also false here —
and indeed the Bose-Mesner is strictly larger than the projector algebra.
The conjecture survives this family **only** because both sides of the
iff are false (not because both are true).
-/

/-- The Xie-Tamon partition sequence: `G_n = K_n ∪ P_n` joined by a single
edge between any vertex of `K_n` and the path endpoint; partition by
distance from `K_n`. -/
noncomputable def Kn_plus_pathn :
    ConsistentPartitionSequence (I := ℕ) (u := 0) := by
  sorry

/-- **Claim (test family 3, "both-false" instance).** Xie-Tamon family:
graphon half is true, chiral half is false, RHS is false, conjecture
holds because both LHS and RHS are false. -/
theorem Kn_plus_pathn_satisfies_conj93 :
    Conjecture93_weak Kn_plus_pathn := by
  -- LHS: admitsGraphonLimit yes (Xie-Tamon explicit limit graphon),
  --      admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition no (tridiagonal tail algebra is
  --      strictly larger than the cell-pair-constant algebra of the
  --      distance partition).
  -- RHS: eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence no (same reason).
  -- So both sides are false; the iff is vacuously true.
  sorry

/-- The Xie-Tamon family does **not** admit a chiral speedup on its
distance partition (this is the substantive content of the family being
a counterexample-shaped instance). -/
theorem Kn_plus_pathn_no_chiral_speedup :
    ¬ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition Kn_plus_pathn := by
  sorry

/-! ### 8.4. Complete multipartite `K_{n,n,n,n}` (four-color completion).

Partition by part. The Bose-Mesner of the four-part complete multipartite
graph is the rank-2 algebra spanned by `I, J_part, J - I - J_part`, where
`J_part` is the within-part all-ones. This equals the cell-pair-constant
algebra of the part partition; algebra coincidence holds.

Both halves of the conjecture hold; this is the "standard positive" four-
color family.
-/

/-- The `K_{n,n,n,n}` family: four parts each of size `n`, partition by
part membership (`I = Fin 4`). -/
noncomputable def K4multipartite (n : ℕ → ℕ) (hn : ∀ k, 0 < n k)
    (h_mono : ∀ k, n k ≤ n (k + 1)) :
    ConsistentPartitionSequence (I := Fin 4) (u := 0) := by
  sorry

/-- **Claim (test family 4).** Complete multipartite `K_{n,n,n,n}` satisfies
the conjecture: both halves hold. -/
theorem K4multipartite_satisfies_conj93
    (n : ℕ → ℕ) (hn : ∀ k, 0 < n k) (h_mono : ∀ k, n k ≤ n (k + 1)) :
    Conjecture93_weak (K4multipartite n hn h_mono) := by
  sorry

/-! ### 8.5. Surface Heawood envelope `g → ∞`.

A consistent partition sequence indexed by genus `g`: at genus `g`, the
ambient graph is the *Heawood envelope*, the complete graph on
`H(g) = ⌊(7 + √(1 + 48 g)) / 2⌋` vertices, with the trivial single-cell
partition.

Limit graphon: the constant kernel `1`. Algebra coincidence: holds
(trivial single-cell partition; both algebras are `ℂ · I + ℂ · J`).
Both halves hold.
-/

/-- The Heawood envelope partition sequence: at stage `g`, complete graph
on `H(g)` vertices with trivial partition. -/
noncomputable def heawoodEnvelope :
    ConsistentPartitionSequence (I := Unit) (u := 0) := by
  sorry

/-- **Claim (test family 5).** The Heawood envelope sequence satisfies the
conjecture: both halves hold via the trivial-partition argument. -/
theorem heawoodEnvelope_satisfies_conj93 :
    Conjecture93_weak heawoodEnvelope := by
  sorry

/-! ### 8.6. **Tight counterexample candidate:** Cayley graphs of `S_n`.

The natural candidate where graphon limit exists but algebra coincidence
*fails*: a sequence of Cayley graphs of `S_n` with a fixed generating
set (say the transpositions). The Bose-Mesner algebra of the
Cayley graph contains all class functions, which is strictly larger than
the conjugacy-class partition projector algebra as soon as a class has
multiple irreducible characters supported in it.

If we take the *conjugacy class partition* `P_n`, then:

* Graphon limit: exists (in the sense of `ConsistentPartitionSequence`
  with appropriate `I` = partition type of `n`).
* Bose-Mesner algebra: equals the convolution algebra of `S_n`, which has
  dimension `∑ d_λ^2 = n!` — much larger than the partition projector
  algebra of dimension `(# classes)^2 = p(n)^2`.
* Hence algebra coincidence **fails** for all `n ≥ 5` (e.g.).

The conjecture predicts: chiral speedup on this partition should **also**
fail (because RHS fails). This is testable.
-/

/-- The Cayley-`S_n`-by-transpositions partition sequence. Stage `n`:
`V_n = S_n`, edges given by multiplication-by-a-transposition. Partition
by conjugacy class. -/
noncomputable def cayleyS_n :
    ConsistentPartitionSequence (I := ℕ) (u := 0) := by
  sorry

/-- **Claim (test family 6, tight counterexample-shaped).** The
Cayley-`S_n` family conjecturally satisfies Conjecture 9.3, because both
LHS and RHS are false (graphon limit exists but chiral speedup on the
conjugacy partition does not; algebra coincidence fails). -/
theorem cayleyS_n_satisfies_conj93 :
    Conjecture93_weak cayleyS_n := by
  sorry

/-- **The substantive content for family 6:** algebra coincidence fails. -/
theorem cayleyS_n_algebra_strictly_larger :
    algebra_strictly_larger cayleyS_n := by
  sorry

/-- And the chiral half also fails — making both sides of the iff false. -/
theorem cayleyS_n_no_chiral_speedup :
    ¬ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition cayleyS_n := by
  sorry

/-! ## 9. The strong-vs-weak gap

We isolate the gap between the **strong** and **weak** versions: any
counterexample to the strong version (LHS holds, RHS fails) must use a
*non-cross-constant* unitary signing.
-/

/-- If the strong conjecture fails on `𝒮` but the weak conjecture holds,
then any witness to the LHS of the strong conjecture must use a unitary
signing that is **not** cross-constant on the cells of `𝒮.cells n`. -/
theorem strong_failure_requires_nonCrossConstant
    (𝒮 : ConsistentPartitionSequence I)
    (h_weak : Conjecture93_weak 𝒮)
    (h_strong_fails : ¬ Conjecture93_strong 𝒮)
    (h_lhs_strong :
      admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 ∧ admitsAnyChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮)
    (h_rhs_fails : ¬ eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence 𝒮) :
    ¬ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮 := by
  -- If `admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮` held, the weak iff would give
  -- `eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence 𝒮`, contradicting `h_rhs_fails`.
  intro h_weak_lhs_chiral
  have h_weak_lhs : admitsGraphonLimit 𝒮 ∧ admitsChiralSpeedupOnPartition 𝒮 :=
    ⟨h_lhs_strong.1, h_weak_lhs_chiral⟩
  have : eventuallyAlgebraCoincidence 𝒮 := h_weak.mp h_weak_lhs
  exact h_rhs_fails this

